417 true] [17592186426369 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426369 1071 "Roy, Kate, and Connor divided $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a watermelon equally among themselves. What part of a watermelon did each of the $3$ friends get?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each of the friends got \n{{field-1}} of a watermelon." 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426369 1072 #uuid "cf6946f6-4d9a-5dfa-9d8c-e7453ac9a280" 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426369 1074 "To determine the part of the watermelon each friend got, we must divide the amount of watermelon by the number of friends.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷3=\\frac{1}{3\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each of the $3$ friends got $\\frac{1}{9}$ of a watermelon." 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426351 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1069 "q-197135" 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1071 "Sam has $\\frac{1}{3}$ cubic meters of wooden boards to make $2$ dog houses. If he uses the same amount of boards for each dog house, how many cubic meters does Sam use for each dog house?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, Sam uses\n{{field-1}} cubic meters of boards for each dog house." 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1072 #uuid "fa95cd0e-dc98-58e2-b9c5-ac52a083197b" 13194139534579 17592186045417 true] [17592186426370 1074 "To determine the amount of boards used for each dog house, we divide the total amount of boards by the number of dog houses.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷2\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷2=\\frac{1}{3\\times 2}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Sam spent $\\frac{1}{6}$ cubic meters